@startuml
title Estimating a population mean from a single random sample
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam activity {
  BackgroundColor #EAF6F0
  BorderColor #2E8B67
}
start
:Estimate how heavy-tailed or skewed\nthe population is (pilot data, domain knowledge);
:Choose sample size n\n(larger for skewed / heavy-tailed data);
:Draw ONE independent random sample\n(random.sample, not a contiguous slice);
:Compute sample mean x and sample SD s;
:Estimate SE = s / sqrt(n);
if (n small?) then (yes)
  :Use Student t quantile instead of 1.96\nand Bessel's n - 1 in s;<<#FFFFFF>>
else (no)
endif
:Report x +/- 1.96 (or t) SE as the 95 % confidence interval;
:Validate by simulation if possible:\nabout 5 % of intervals should miss mu;
stop
@enduml
